From b004af1eb7e1ca06c85a356719be6ed03a441e59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <will-tm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:05:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 159/161] hw/gpio: imx_gpio: read back driven outputs in PSR

PSR masked out the output bits, so a line configured as an output read
back 0 whatever DR drove. A GPIO pad keeps its input path, and Linux's
gpio-mxc reads every line's value from PSR: the stock Onyx nlclient
checks its backplate reset line through sysfs after driving it, and
reported "failed to set the backplate hard reset Gpio back to 0" on
every hard reset (the line is active low).

PSR now returns DR for outputs and the input level for inputs, as DR
reads already do.
---
 hw/gpio/imx_gpio.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/gpio/imx_gpio.c b/hw/gpio/imx_gpio.c
index 5abf208..712bf7f 100644
--- a/hw/gpio/imx_gpio.c
+++ b/hw/gpio/imx_gpio.c
@@ -160,7 +160,11 @@ static uint64_t imx_gpio_read(void *opaque, hwaddr offset, unsigned size)
         break;
 
     case PSR_ADDR:
-        reg_value = s->psr & ~s->gdir;
+        /*
+         * The pad's level: a GPIO pad keeps its input path, so an output
+         * reads back what DR drives (Linux's gpio-mxc reads outputs here).
+         */
+        reg_value = (s->dr & s->gdir) | (s->psr & ~s->gdir);
         break;
 
     case ICR1_ADDR:
